{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: restore the proper-prefix batch recovery regression required by closed #894. Take this bounded test follow-up after the completed receipt-regression delivery #21317 (the current-basis successor of #20513), then return to the full I7 commitment; preserve I7, independent reviews and every other promised outcome. If an earlier source item has already begun, finish that item first and state the resulting queue position.\n\nThe [current test](cmd/gs/main_test.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:3507) retains a partial-landing name but now checks preflight refusal with zero events, a complete landing, and a complete replay. It never enters the mixed replay/new-append case still promised by the [batch contract](docs/reference/gs/batch.md@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:104). The [current implementation](cmd/gs/main.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:1822) passes an isolated real-prefix probe.\n\nThe [evidence](batch-prefix-evidence.json), [probe](batch-prefix-probe_test.go) and [compiled mutant](mixed-outcome-mutant.diff) show the gap: the existing named test passes when mixed replay/new-suffix results are deliberately rejected, while the probe fails. This recovers missing assurance; no runtime defect or need for a kernel change has been established.\n\nAuthor replacement of stale #21305 before implementation. The performer, full conditions below, main destination, historical retirement basis and all three original evidence attachments are retained. The test-file basis now names the actual publication from landed #21317. The other two exact-path source artifacts are live and their bytes match examined main 98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7. Ordinary inherited staleness remains recorded rather than erasing provenance. The historical probe results stay attributed to their original examined head; no fresh runtime execution is claimed by this author refresh.\n\nThe [current numbered test excerpt](batch-prefix-current-test-excerpt.txt) shows the unchanged test at its new line location. Its entire function is byte-identical to the earlier examined main a6ed642f; only surrounding receipt-test work changed the file. The [reconciliation](batch-prefix-current-reconciliation.json) records exact source hashes. All completion, independent review, signed admission, omission sensitivity, idempotency, landing, push, CI and cleanup conditions remain owed. This task does not reopen the historically delivered batch feature or authorize live batch replay.\n\nThe agreed start condition is now met: #21317 is sealed, pushed, green in CI and Security, and its owned worktree and branch are gone. This proceeds under Codex's already-confirmed availability and agreed queue. Claim this successor, complete its reviewed delivery, then return to full I7.","body":{"branch":"request/batch-prefix-recovery-regression","conditions":"From then-current main in a new request/batch-prefix-recovery-regression worktree, preserve the useful current preflight-refusal and complete-replay controls, and give their test/comment an accurate name. Add a direct proper-prefix recovery test: durably seed only the first act of a valid two-or-more-act batch using its actual idempotency key, then submit the complete unchanged chain. Assert replayed prefix plus newly landed suffix, exact original prefix event identity, suffix provenance to that exact prefix, typed per-act outcomes and aggregate counts, exactly the missing depth increment, and no duplicate prefix. Retry the entire batch again and assert all events replay, exact identities are retained and head/depth do not move. Exercise the real existing batch/fixture and signed append path; do not replace it with a report-only mock. Keep independent labels, malformed-input, kernel admission and preflight behavior intact. A deterministic isolated prefix seed meets the original condition; do not invent production crash machinery just to create it.\n\nDemonstrate that the added